From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElXreno <elxreno@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:37:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: keep the plane ILUT in sync with the CRTC
 DEGAMMA_LUT

From ElXreno, upstream PR 1506, commit 6c4f9dee. The PR's second commit is
not needed: "fix color pipeline state handling" already stops the ILUT
rebuild on every commit, and that is what exposed these bugs for clients
with DRM_CLIENT_CAP_PLANE_COLOR_PIPELINE set.

The legacy CRTC DEGAMMA_LUT is programmed as each plane's ILUT, but
plane_req_config_update() only rebuilds the ILUT surface when the plane's
own degamma properties or the CRTC's color management changed in this
commit, and only sends it to NVKMS when the plane's degamma properties
changed or the previous request had no ILUT.

Three cases are lost:

- A plane attached to a CRTC whose DEGAMMA_LUT was set in an earlier commit
  never gets an ILUT, so the CTM runs on encoded values and GAMMA_LUT
  encodes them a second time.
- Removing the CRTC's DEGAMMA_LUT drops the ILUT surface but never sends the
  disabled ILUT, so the hardware keeps linearizing with the old LUT.
- Replacing the CRTC's DEGAMMA_LUT builds a new surface but never sends it.

In the last two cases the old surface also goes back to the LUT pool while
the request still points at it.

Rebuild the ILUT when the plane moves onto a CRTC, as is already done for
the CSC, and send it whenever it was rebuilt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 71f4cb64..28b207d8 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -1246,6 +1246,7 @@ plane_req_config_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
     struct nv_drm_plane_state *nv_drm_plane_state =
         to_nv_drm_plane_state(plane_state);
     bool matrix_overrides_changed = 0;
+    bool degamma_rebuilt = false;
 
     if (plane_state->fb == NULL) {
         plane_req_config_disable(req_config);
@@ -1566,7 +1567,10 @@ plane_req_config_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
                                &matrix_overrides_changed);
     req_config->flags.matrixOverridesChanged = matrix_overrides_changed;
 
-    if (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_changed || crtc_state->color_mgmt_changed) {
+    if (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_changed || crtc_state->color_mgmt_changed ||
+        (plane->state->crtc != plane_state->crtc)) {
+        degamma_rebuilt = true;
+
         if (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_drm_lut_surface != NULL) {
             kref_put(&nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_drm_lut_surface->base.refcount,
                      release_drm_lut_surface);
@@ -1593,11 +1597,13 @@ plane_req_config_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
     /*
      * Send ILUT configuration to NVKMS if:
      * - degamma properties changed, OR
+     * - the ILUT was rebuilt above, which includes the CRTC's DEGAMMA_LUT
+     *   being changed or removed, OR
      * - plane is being re-enabled and old req_config had ILUT disabled
      *   but DRM plane state has ILUT (blob ID didn't change, but NVKMS
      *   needs to be notified)
      */
-    if (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_changed ||
+    if (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_changed || degamma_rebuilt ||
         (!old_config.ilut.enabled && (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_drm_lut_surface != NULL))) {
 
         if (nv_drm_plane_state->degamma_drm_lut_surface != NULL) {
